Next Topic: Docker – Single Container Application
Aim: To create a Docker image, run a container, and access an application using Docker.
Step 1: Install Docker Desktop
1. Download Docker Desktop from https://www.docker.com/products/docker-desktop/
2. Install Docker Desktop.
3. Restart your computer if required.
4. Open Docker Desktop.
5. Wait until Docker Engine is running.
Step 2: Open Command Prompt
Check Docker installation:
docker --version


Check whether Docker is running:
docker info


Step 3: Create a project folder
mkdir DockerProject
cd DockerProject


Step 4: Create an HTML file
Create a file named index.html inside the DockerProject folder.

Write the following code:
<html>
<head>
    <title>Docker Application</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Welcome to Docker</h1>
    <p>My first Docker container application.</p>
</body>
</html>


Step 5: Create a Dockerfile
Inside the same folder, create a file named Dockerfile (without any extension).

Write:
FROM nginx:latest

COPY index.html /usr/share/nginx/html/index.html

EXPOSE 80


Explanation:
- FROM: Specifies the base image.
- COPY: Copies the HTML file into the container.
- EXPOSE: Documents the port used by the application.
Step 6: Build Docker image
Execute:
docker build -t mywebapp .


This creates a Docker image named mywebapp.
Step 7: Check Docker images
docker images


You should see mywebapp in the list.
Step 8: Run Docker container
docker run -d -p 8080:80 --name mycontainer mywebapp


Explanation:
- -d: Runs container in the background.
- -p: Maps host port 8080 to container port 80.
- --name: Assigns a name to the container.
Step 9: Check running containers
docker ps


You should see mycontainer with status Up.
Step 10: Open application in browser
Open:
http://localhost:8080


You should see:

Welcome to Docker
Step 11: Stop and remove container
Stop the container:
docker stop mycontainer


Remove the container:
docker rm mycontainer


Remove the image:
docker rmi mywebapp


